  "note": "Complete principal Christiansborg Palace exterior and exact-way connected riding complex: high asymmetric U, central through-passage/tower, both returned wings/lower risalits, attached low links, complete curved stables/inner arcades and twin riding halls, pitched roofs/dormers/chimneys, recessed white-grid glazing/closed arcade backs and original simplified trim. Tower has a stone base,real open lower arched gallery,curved metal shoulders,open upper lantern,small gold accents andthree original green crown/finial silhouettes. Main court/riding grounds remain open; separate chapel432/437,archive-side gallery516,city andcanals remain native. No copied figures,heraldry,text orinteriors. Approximate9m standard global DEM reference,main-palace floor11.8m andlow riding-ground floor6.7m. Main eaves28.8m/roof38.6m,low arcades7.7m/roof13.5m,twin halls25.3m andtower105.3m are map/picture-guided heights above that approximate datum. Low facade bases follow a bounded graded plinth between high court andlow riding precinct while roof levels remain fixed. Three small supported approaches use actual standard terrain profiles; the portal floor andlarge open precinct stay native. No surveyed historic elevations orflattened precinct is claimed. +X SSE across the principal palace range; +Z WSW toward open main court and riding grounds; -Z ENE toward outer Slotsplads. +Y up."
